<%# THE FOCUS GAME — the one game the reader is watching, at full size.
    Locals: games (enumerable of Game), focus_slug (String or nil).

    EVERY GAME IS RENDERED HERE AND ALL BUT ONE IS HIDDEN, the same bargain the
    contest live page strikes (contests/_live_focus) and for the same reasons:
    fetching the chosen game on click needs a route, a frame and a spinner
    between the click and the picture, and the next broadcast would overwrite
    that frame with whichever game the SERVER thought was interesting. Rendering
    all of them makes switching instant and makes a score reach the focused game
    and the fifteen you might switch to by exactly the same path as everything
    else on the page — the broadcast that replaces this whole panel.

    WHAT IS DIFFERENT HERE: the focused game is REMOVED FROM THE GRID below
    (live/_scoreboard hides it with the same `focus` state), so it appears
    exactly once on the page. On the contest page the strip is a chooser and
    keeps every chip; here the grid IS the list of games, and a game drawn both
    as a hero and as a card two inches below it reads as a duplicate.

    The inline `display:none` is not belt-and-braces for x-show. Alpine boots
    after first paint, so without it the page opens with a column of sixteen
    hero tiles that then collapses to one. %>
<% if games.any? %>
  <% games.each do |game| %>
    <div x-show="focus === '<%= game.slug %>'"
         data-test="live-focus-game"
         data-focus-slug="<%= game.slug %>"
         style="<%= "display: none" unless game.slug == focus_slug %>">
      <%= render "live/game_tile", game: game, scorers: true, size: :hero %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
